    "created_at": "2017-03-27T10:11:54Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-27T10:11:54Z",
    "body": "Isn't this behavior the same for other things, like fonts, stylesheets, scripts?\r\n\r\nThe intent as far as the spec for `img` goes is that the logic for reusing an ongoing fetch is the responsibility of the Fetch spec, and the \"list of available images\" is layered on top and only populated for completed fetches with decodable images. (There is an [open bug about extending it to cover unsuccessful image fetches](https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=25798) as well, to avoid retrying over and over.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
